Owner·Admin 은 기본적으로 `access_all=true` 다. 그래서 이 세 핸들러의
`if member.access_all { continue; }` 는 그들의 명시적 `users_collections` 행을
**아예 만들지 않는다.** 그런데 하류 권한 판정(`get_access_restrictions`)은 여전히
그 행을 찾는다.

증상이 권한 오류처럼 안 생긴다는 게 이 결함의 성질이다:
  · Owner 가 자기가 만든 cipher 를 삭제하지 못한다(`permissions.delete` 가 false 로 계산)
  · `bw` CLI 의 `collection edit` / `cipher delete` 가 서버 에러 없이 조용히 실패한다

이미 전체 접근 권한을 가진 멤버에게 그 행을 하나 더 써 두는 것은 무해하다 —
비용은 행 하나이고, 얻는 것은 두 권한 경로의 일치다.

구 시리즈 0003 의 재작성이다(베이스가 v2026.7.0-1 로 올라가며 컨텍스트가 어긋났다).
---
 src/api/core/organizations.rs | 25 ++++++++++++++++---------
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/api/core/organizations.rs b/src/api/core/organizations.rs
index ebe9c1d..1b44dca 100644
--- a/src/api/core/organizations.rs
+++ b/src/api/core/organizations.rs
@@ -544,9 +544,13 @@ async fn post_organization_collections(
             err!("User is not part of organization")
         };
 
-        if member.access_all {
-            continue;
-        }
+        // axe: do NOT skip access_all members here. Owner/Admin carry access_all=true by
+        // default, so skipping means their explicit `users_collections` row is never
+        // written — while downstream permission checks (get_access_restrictions) still
+        // look for that row. The visible damage is an Owner who cannot delete their own
+        // cipher and a `bw` CLI whose `collection edit` fails with no server error.
+        // Writing the row is harmless for members who already have blanket access.
+
 
         CollectionUser::save(
             &member.user_uuid,
@@ -622,9 +626,8 @@ async fn post_bulk_access_collections(
                 err!("User is not part of organization")
             };
 
-            if member.access_all {
-                continue;
-            }
+            // axe: see the note above — access_all members still need the explicit row.
+
 
             CollectionUser::save(&member.user_uuid, &col_id, user.read_only, user.hide_passwords, user.manage, &conn)
                 .await?;
@@ -701,9 +704,13 @@ async fn post_organization_collection_update(
             err!("User is not part of organization")
         };
 
-        if member.access_all {
-            continue;
-        }
+        // axe: do NOT skip access_all members here. Owner/Admin carry access_all=true by
+        // default, so skipping means their explicit `users_collections` row is never
+        // written — while downstream permission checks (get_access_restrictions) still
+        // look for that row. The visible damage is an Owner who cannot delete their own
+        // cipher and a `bw` CLI whose `collection edit` fails with no server error.
+        // Writing the row is harmless for members who already have blanket access.
+
 
         CollectionUser::save(&member.user_uuid, &col_id, user.read_only, user.hide_passwords, user.manage, &conn)
             .await?;
